\"`>=`\",\n            Tok::LParen => \"`(`\",\n","metadata":{"output":"\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]\nenum Tok {\n    Str(String),\n    Int(i64),\n    Ident(String),\n    Fn,\n    Pub,\n    Type,\n    Enum,\n    If,\n    Else,\n    Stdin,\n    And,\n    Or,\n    Not,\n    Plus,\n    Minus,\n    Star,\n    Slash,\n    Percent,\n    Pipe,\n    Comma,\n    Dot,\n    Eq,\n    EqEq,\n    Ne,\n    Bang,\n    Lt,\n    Le,\n    Gt,\n    Ge,\n    LParen,\n    RParen,\n    LBracket,\n    RBracket,\n    LBrace,\n    RBrace,\n    Colon,\n    Arrow,\n    Eof,\n}\n\nimpl std::fmt::Display for Tok {\n    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> std::fmt::Result {\n        let s = match self {\n            Tok::Str(_) => return write!(f, \"a string\"),\n            Tok::Int(n) => return write!(f, \"`{n}`\"),\n            Tok::Ident(name) => return write!(f, \"`{name}`\"),\n            Tok::Fn => \"`fn`\",\n            Tok::Pub => \"`pub`\",\n            Tok::Type => \"`type`\",\n            Tok::Enum => \"`enum`\",\n            Tok::If => \"`if`\",\n            Tok::Else => \"`else`\",\n            Tok::Stdin => \"`stdin`\",\n            Tok::And => \"`and`\",\n            Tok::Or => \"`or`\",\n            Tok::Not => \"`not`\",\n            Tok::Plus => \"`+`\",\n            Tok::Minus => \"`-`\",\n            Tok::Star => \"`*`\",\n            Tok::Slash => \"`/`\",\n            Tok::Percent => \"`%`\",\n            Tok::Pipe => \"`|`\",\n            Tok::Comma => \"`,`\",\n            Tok::Dot => \"`.`\",\n            Tok::Eq => \"`=`\",\n            Tok::EqEq => \"`==`\",\n            Tok::Ne => \"`!=`\",\n            Tok::Bang => \"`!`\",\n            Tok::Lt => \"`<`\",\n            Tok::Le => \"`<=`\",\n            Tok::Gt => \"`>`\",\n            Tok::Ge => \"`>=`\",\n            Tok::LParen => \"`(`\",\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git show HEAD:src/parse.rs | sed -n '35,110p'","time":{"start":1788372391029,"end":1788372391034}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"OK so the diff of working-tree parse.rs vs HEAD shows a big change: the working tree added `Let`, `Dsv`, `Csv`, `Tsv` tokens, plus an `input <type>` annotation block, etc. Wait -- this is the diff showing what the working tree has compared to HEAD. So the current working tree (as edited by prior runs) has ADDED Let/Dsv/Csv/Tsv tokens and an input annotation. Hmm, this seems like the merge resolution the prior agent did was quite extensive, OR... wait.\n\n\n\nHold on. Let me re-think. `git diff HEAD -- src/parse.rs` shows working tree vs HEAD (our branch, pre-merge). HEAD is our branch issue-159's version. The working tree is the conflicted state as edited by prior runs.\n\n. The diff shows lines being ADDED in the working tree (with `+` prefix) and REMOVED (with `-`).\n\nLooking at the diff: working tree added `Let`, `Dsv`, `Csv`, `Tsv` tokens; removed `If`, `Else`?? No wait -- the diff hunk:\n\n```\n-    Enum,\n-    If,\n-    Else,\n+Enum,\n+    Let,\n     Stdin,\n+    Dsv,\n+    Csv,\n+    Tsv,\n```\n\nHmm. The `-` lines are HEAD's content; the `+` lines are working-tree content. So HEAD (our branch) had `Enum, If, Else,` (with indentation) in the enum; working tree has `Enum,` (unindented!? odd, Let, Stdin, Dsv, Csv, Tsv`. \n\nWait, that's weird: it looks like HEAD already had Let? No -- HEAD had `If, Else,` and NO Let... hmm but earlier I saw HEAD's enum at line  ǅ47 had `Stdin,` and the grep for Stdin in HEAD showed lines 47, 90, 178, 1209. Let me look at HEAD's actual enum definition.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0634d145b0016Jj5QiczpLlub6","sessionID":"ses_f9cb37b32ffekf1PK55ZywltbG","messageID":"msg_0634cffea001jUhSfb6zs1FFg1"}}
