{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788372442598,"sessionID":"ses_f9cb37b32ffekf1PK55ZywltbG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_4f7b04884f28439e8de549c9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git merge-base HEAD origin/main"},"output":"7c4cc863541c149620a2347c0489f1e0d2548dde\n","metadata":{"output":"7c4cc863541c149620a2347c0489f1e0d2548dde\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git merge-base HEAD origin/main","time":{"start":1788372442591,"end":1788372442593}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"OK. HEAD's tir.rs has `Kind::Stdin` and `Source::Stdin`. HEAD's parse.rs has only Stdin keyword. So our branch's model: single stdin source.\n\nOrigin/main's tir.rs presumably has Source::Input/Inputs/Lines/... Let me check origin/main's tir.rs and src/tir.rs working tree. Also let me check the other files. The key insight: I need to reconstruct the merge consistently across ALL files. This is a big task. Let me approach it systematically.\n\nLet me understand what origin/main changed overall vs the merge base, and what our branch changed. The merge base is the common ancestor. Let me find it and compare.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0634dddc3001qc78LXa18XhQuJ","sessionID":"ses_f9cb37b32ffekf1PK55ZywltbG","messageID":"msg_0634dd617001C0Lz6sNTlGMKG3"}}
