ind::Var(name) => Base::Var(name),\n         Kind::Local(id) => Base::Local(*id),\n         Kind::Bind { local, value, body } => {\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git diff origin/main -- src/tir.rs | head -120","time":{"start":1788372504148,"end":1788372504150}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I have the whole tir.rs. Let me write the merged file. Resolutions:\n\nBlock 1 (lines  ǅ61-76):\n```\n    /// The one source:the stream of raw lines read from stdin, born `Stream<Str>``.\n    Stdin,\n    /// Stdin read as raw lines, each split on the delimiter, born `Vec<Vec<Str>>`:the\n    /// parameterized DSV source. `csv`/`tsv` arrive here with the delimiter already fixed.\n    Dsv {\n        delim: String,\n    },\n```\n\nBlock 2 (lines  ǅ278-294):\n```\n    /// Whether the program reads `stdin`. A stream is read at most once,and the flag is what\n    /// lets the host connect the real stdin through rather than pre-reading it.\n    pub uses_stdin: bool,\n    /// The delimiter the program splits raw lines on, if it reads `dsv`/`csv`/`tsv`. It\n    /// reads the same real stdin as the source,so it is exclusive with it.\n    pub dsv: Option<String>,\n```\n\nBlock  ǅ3 (lines  ǅ331-347):\n```\n/// What a fused loop reads one entry at a time: a raw line of stdin,to be parsed by whatever\n/// `parse` calls sit in the stages,or integers counted out of a `range` call.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\npub enum Source<'a> {\n    Stdin,\n    /// `range(n)` with its already-checked bound `n`, evaluated once before the loop runs.\n\n    Range(&'a Tir),\n}\n```\n\nWait, the original theirs block:\n```\n/// What a fused loop reads one entry at a time: parsed JSON values, raw lines, or integers\n/// counted out of a `range` call.\n#[derive(Clone, Copy)]\npub enum Source<'a> {\n    Inputs,\n    Lines,\n    /// `range(n)` with its already-checked bound `n`, evaluated once before the loop runs.\n    Range(&'a Tir),\n}\n```\n\nOurs:\n```\n//