ke `->` and `--`? The AGENTS.md says plain ASCII. The existing file uses `->` (arrow-> ok ascii), and \"—\"? Let me check: line  ǅ50 has \"(kantord/toylang#47's totality round owns that)\" -- uses apostrophes normal. Line  ǅ155 \"(kantord/toylang#143), jq's `.[a:b]`; `None`\" -- there's a `;` weird. Hmm, these are existing quirks from prior content (the file seems to use `;` oddly instead of punctuation... whatever, I preserve the exact content as read.\n\nWait, looking closely at the read output, there are odd semicolons scattered: e.g. line  ǅ32: \"in the type. That is what lets a backend address one by index rather than\" -- normal. But line  ǅ37-38: \"the variant's position (its tag,where one is needed) and its payload type by asking `ty::variants`\". Hmm, these might be rendering artifacts of the read tool replacing some characters? Actually no, the read tool shows the literal file content. The file probably genuinely contains these odd semicolons (maybe a prior agent corrupted it? Or the original genuinely has them?\n\nWait, let me compare with origin/main's tir.rs to see if these oddities exist there. Let me check a sample. Actually, I worry that the prior agent corrupted non-conflict regions with weird punctuation (maybe a bad sed?). Let me diff the working tree tir.rs against origin/main's to see the oddities.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0634ece45001X5xk0UOW90YjMl","sessionID":"ses_f9cb37b32ffekf1PK55ZywltbG","messageID":"msg_0634ea57e0018441nCYz3F96qR"}}
