laration feature but rework it? Our retirement explicitly removed the annotation feature in check/mod.rs (the commit removed the `input` field from Ctx and `Expr::Input` handling... and `input_read`). And the annotation was for `input`, so it's gone.\n\n. So merged check/mod.rs = origin/main's check/mod.rs, minus all input/inputs/lines machinery and the annotation feature, plus stdin_used and parse handling. Plus everything else origin/main added (Float? etc. \n\nWait, but hold on: what about origin/main's `file.input` (the annotation in the AST)? Origin/main's ast.rs has an `input: Option<Type>` on File? Our commit modified ast.rs (Exported Input/Inputs/Lines Expr variants → Stdin,. So the merged ast.rs = origin/main's ast.rs with Input/Inputs/Lines→Stdin in the Expr enum. And origin/main's File probably has `input: Option<Type>` annotation field. Our branch's File... let me check our HEAD's ast.rs for `input` annotation. Actually our commit's ast.rs diff only touched the Expr enum (Input/Inputs/Lines→Stdin)and `Expr::span` match. If the base already had `File.input` (the annotation feature existed in the base?, then our retirement commit would have had to remove it...). Let me check the base's ast.rs.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0634fdae6001jR7KLFtPTcQhBO","sessionID":"ses_f9cb37b32ffekf1PK55ZywltbG","messageID":"msg_0634fc93a001po0pp4WHmfaEbt"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788372572937,"sessionID":"ses_f9cb37b32ffekf1PK55ZywltbG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_3f715523734545c48c363d86","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git show origin/main:src/ast.rs | grep -n 'input\\|Input\\|lines\\|Lines\\|annotation' | head -30"},"output":"99:    /// `Stream<T>`, legal only as the whole of a parameter or return annotation: a stream is\n189:    /// `input <type>`: a declaration of what stdin holds, written after the definitions and\n191:    /// the input untyped, in which case the first use of `input` in the body types it.\n192:    pub input: Option<TypeExpr>,\n296:    Input {\n300:    /// Like `input`, its element type comes only from where it is used.\n301:    Inputs {\n304:    /// The stream of lines read from stdin, born `Stream<Str>`. The checker rejects a second\n306:    Lines {\n309:    /// Stdin read as raw lines, each split on a delimiter, born `Vec<Vec<Str>>`: the\n431:            | Expr::Input { span }\n432:            | Expr::Inputs { span }\n433:            | Expr::Lines { span }\n","metadata":{"output":"99:    /// `Stream<T>`, legal only as the whole of a parameter or return annotation: a stream is\n189:    /// `input <type>`: a declaration of what stdin holds, written after the definitions and\n191:    /// the input untyped, in which case the first use of `input` in the body types it.\n192:    pub input: Option<TypeExpr>,\n296:    Input {\n300:    /// Like `input`, its element type comes only from where it is used.\n301:    Inputs {\n304:    /// The stream of lines read from stdin, born `Stream<Str>`. The checker rejects a second\n306:    Lines {\n309:    /// Stdin read as raw lines, each split on a delimiter, born `Vec<Vec<Str>>`: the\n431:            | Expr::Input { span }\n432:            | Expr::Inputs { span }\n433:            | Expr::Lines { span }\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"git show origin/main:src/ast.rs | grep -n 'input\\|Input\\|lines\\|Lines\\